course: dictionary
lesson: 10365
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Traveller can mean a person who goes on a trip from one place to another. It can also mean a passenger on a bus, train or plane.
explain: «Travellers to some countries need extra vaccines or medicines.» The clue is "to some countries": these travellers are people going on trips abroad. Swap in your meaning, "people going on trips", and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters and wider context also help. In Ireland and the UK, Travellers with a capital T are a community with their own traditions, and many have lived moving from place to place. So the meaning depends on the sentence, not only on the spelling.
fact: A traveller is a person who goes on a trip from one place to another, or who travels a lot.
fact: A traveller can also be a passenger on a bus, train or plane.
fact: Travellers with a capital T, in Ireland and the UK, are a community with their own traditions.
fact: «Wayfarers» means travellers on foot, people on their way somewhere.
fact: Phrases such as «a seasoned traveller» and «a time traveller» use the word in a special way.
exercise: «Travellers to some countries need extra vaccines or medicines.» What does traveller mean here? | Old stories about kings | *People who go on trips to other countries | Animals that move from place to place | People who sell medicines in a shop
exercise: «The traveller greets the Rat with a gesture of courtesy.» What is the traveller in this story? | *A person on a journey who meets a Rat | A ticket for a train | A kind of cat that lives in the forest | A bus driver who stops for a rest
exercise: The chapter's name is «Wayfarers All»: wayfarers are travellers on foot. Find and copy the word that means people walking on their way somewhere. | chapter | All | name | *wayfarers
test: «The travellers waited at the airport gate for the flight.» What does traveller mean here? | Drivers who fix the planes | Animals that fly south in winter | *Passengers waiting to board a plane | Shops that sell gates
test: Which phrase uses traveller to mean someone who has made many trips? | a fellow pencil | *a seasoned traveller | a hot cup of tea | a sleepy cat
exam: Dani reads «In Ireland and the UK, Travellers are a community with their own traditions.» What does Travellers mean here? | A type of ticket | A passenger on a bus | *A community of people with their own traditions | A word for lost property
